# FR : lit le plan SVG d'un composant et rend ses courbes nommées en mètres, dans le repère de l'objet.
#
# A blueprint is one SVG file, in millimetres, with one <g> per view. Each view group says how its 2D axes map to
# the world through data-map, for example data-map="x:-z,y:-y" for a side view (screen x is minus world z, screen y
# is minus world y, SVG y pointing down). Named <path id="..."> elements are the key curves of the component; an
# optional <image> is the original reference photo placed under them. The file is text with numbers in mm, so it is
# code: Claude edits it, Matthieu can edit it in any vector editor, and the builder reads it back.
# Supported path commands: M L H V C S Q T Z, absolute and relative. Path coordinates are the group's LOCAL millimetres,
# which are the world millimetres of that view: a group transform only places the view on the page and is ignored.
# 9 November 2026: corrected, the first version subtracted the group translation and moved the hood by 2.2 m.
